{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Blessed shall you be, etc.</b> Meaning, that you shall not be a nation smaller than them. Or it may intend along this line — <b>blessed shall you be</b>, etc., and what is the blessing? That there shall not be, etc. And His saying ״among you״, etc., means that no man will be found barren of himself, and corresponding to barrenness that comes by way of illness He said <b>and HaShem will remove from you every illness</b> — and in this the blessing of ״there shall be no barren one among you״ will be recognizable, when there will be no man in Israel who does not beget." "<b>Further,</b> He may intend by saying <b>and He will remove</b>, etc., in the manner of their saying, of blessed memory (Ketubot 30a): ״All is in the hands of Heaven except colds and fevers״, etc. Therefore He said ״and He will remove״ — meaning, since these are not in His hand and come upon a man, He promises that He will remove them after they have already come. And corresponding to illnesses that come through an agent He said <b>He will not put them upon you</b>, and therefore He was not satisfied with the statement ״and He will remove״ and needed to repeat and say ״He will not put them,״ and did not rely on what He had previously said, ״and He will remove.״" "<b>Further,</b> he comes to awaken recognition of the kindness of El, for it is He who removes illness from Israel — lest they say that the matter comes according to nature, that there are times and seasons when there are no illnesses in the world. Therefore He said <b>and every disease</b>, etc. <b>He will not put them upon you, but will lay them upon all</b>, etc., and through this you will understand that the matter comes through divine providence from HaShem, and the miracle will be recognized." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend that even though HaShem will place the diseases upon their enemies — the illness will not cling from them to Israel, even if it is an infectious disease like a ra'atan disease (Avodah Zarah 13a), HaShem will make a distinction between Israel and the nations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The word ״הסובב״ (surrounding) appears in the lemma from והסיר ה׳ ממך כל חולי; the surrounding sickness, i.e. illness that encircles/afflicts a person."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:51.006169442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}